
### Collection conventions

| Kind | `name` | `path` | `match` | `ui.router` |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Page singleton | `home`, `mission`, `therapy` | `content/pages` | `{ include: "<filename-without-ext>" }` | `singletonUi("/route")` |
| Document list | `clinicians`, `trustees` | `content/<folder>` | none | `({ document }) => /<folder>/${document._sys.filename}` |
| Shared blocks | `shared` | `content/shared` | none | no router; create/delete off |

Query names are derived from `name`:

- singleton `home` → `client.queries.home({ relativePath: "home.json" })`
- singleton `crisisSupport` with `match.include: "crisis-support"` → `client.queries.crisisSupport({ relativePath: "crisis-support.json" })`
- list `clinicians` → `client.queries.clinicians({ relativePath: "${slug}.json" })`
- list connection → `client.queries.cliniciansConnection()`

`relativePath` is always the filename inside that collection’s `path`, including `.json`.

